--- FINDING: apps/mcp/src/claim-receipt.test.ts has a pre-existing authoring bug ---
Every test body under the outer describe('kaola-mcp Claim recovery receipt (Issue #32)', ...)
references a module-level identifier 'mod' (e.g. mod.receiptFilePath, mod.runStdioBridge)
that is NEVER declared anywhere in the file. loadBridge() (which performs the dynamic
import) is called and its result discarded at line 813; no 'const mod = await loadBridge()'
exists at any scope. This throws 'ReferenceError: mod is not defined' regardless of what
apps/mcp/src/main.ts exports -- confirmed unchanged (still 1 pass / 25 fail) against my
completed implementation. This is a test-authoring defect, not a production gap; per my
role I have not edited the test file. See 'AS-IS RUN' below for the unmodified suite, and
'PATCHED VERIFICATION RUN' for evidence the production code is otherwise fully correct.

A second, independent test bug was found only visible once the first is patched: the
'boundary: receipt written but request never reached the server' test (around line 664)
calls writeFileSync(receiptPathBefore, ...) directly without first creating the parent
receipts/<origin-hash>/ directory, unlike the corruption tests a few hundred lines later
which correctly call mkdirSync(dirname(path), { recursive: true }) first. Against a fresh
tmpKaolaHome (no prior receipts dir for that origin) this throws ENOENT from the test's own
setup code, not from apps/mcp/src/main.ts. Also reported as a finding, not edited.

